# Test files that must not run while any other file is running.
#
# `scripts/parallel_pytest.py` runs one process per file, and these get the
# machine to themselves before the rest start. Blank lines and # comments are
# ignored.

# Writes real folders into `tracks/` and takes them away again - which is the
# only honest way to test that a broken folder cannot take the pool down with
# it. Every other test file does `import tracks` at module scope, and the pool
# is assembled once, at that import. A file that imports while a scratch folder
# is on disk gets it *in the pool*, so `test_tracks.py` then parametrizes its
# whole suite over a track called `zzscratch` and fails on it. Filtering the
# listing is not enough (see `conftest.track_folders`), because this arrives
# through the assembled pool rather than through a listing.
test_track_folders.py
